wayfarmap.gui.iso=3D map (isometric, like Dynmap)
wayfarmap.gui.iso_hint=3D: Q / E turn the view
wayfarmap.gui.iso_not_recording=Block recording is off: new places on the 3D map are drawn from the flat map (settings, 3D map tab)
wayfarmap.option.map.isoCaptureMs=Chunk copying, ms per tick
wayfarmap.option.map.isoCaptureMs.desc=Time per game tick spent copying the blocks of loaded chunks into the 3D map. More puts new chunks on it sooner, but may cost frames while flying over new land.
wayfarmap.option.map.isoOverhangDepth=Look under roofs
wayfarmap.option.map.isoOverhangDepth.desc=How many blocks under a roof or an overhang the 3D map keeps, so the space under it is not drawn as solid stone from the side. 0 = off. More takes more memory. Applies as chunks are copied again.
wayfarmap.option.logs.log3d=3D map log
wayfarmap.option.logs.log3d.desc=Write a detailed log of how chunks get onto the 3D map (.minecraft/wayfarmap/logs/3d-*.log), to find out why some take long. Takes effect when a world is joined.
wayfarmap.option.logs.log2d=Flat map log
wayfarmap.option.logs.log2d.desc=Write a detailed log of the flat map (.minecraft/wayfarmap/logs/2d-*.log): chunks scanned, regions read from and saved to disk, textures and drawing. Takes effect when a world is joined.
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadServerMs=Server time per tick, ms
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadServerMs.desc=Milliseconds of each server tick spent loading and generating chunks for /wf chunkload. More maps an area faster; on a shared server less keeps the TPS up (in single player the server has time to spare).
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadBatch=Batch size, chunks
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadBatch.desc=Chunks per side of a batch. Bigger batches load fewer chunks twice (each batch loads a ring of one chunk around it) and wait less for the client, but hold more chunks in memory. Used by the next command started.
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadClientMs=Client time per tick, ms
wayfarmap.option.commands.chunkloadClientMs.desc=Milliseconds of each client tick spent putting the chunks of a batch on the map.
